Parse once, fetch a unit

Soft PHP — no Composer, no YAML library required for flat keys:
```
/** Split chip text into meta map + body */
function chipParse(string $raw): array {
  $meta = [];
  $body = $raw;

  if (preg_match('/^---\s*\R(.*?)\R---\s*\R?(.*)\z/s', $raw, $m)) {
    $head = $m[1];
    $body = $m[2];
    foreach (preg_split('/\R/', $head) as $line) {
      $line = trim($line);
      if ($line === '' || str_starts_with($line, '#')) continue;
      // "title: Hello stars"
      if (preg_match('/^([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)\s*:\s*(.*)$/', $line, $kv)) {
        $meta[$kv[1]] = trim($kv[2]);
      }
    }
  }
  return ['meta' => $meta, 'body' => $body, 'raw' => $raw];
}

/** One unit of information */
function chipGet(array $chip, string $key, $default = null) {
  if ($key === 'body') return $chip['body'] ?? $default;
  if ($key === 'raw')  return $chip['raw'] ?? $default;
  return $chip['meta'][$key] ?? $default;
}
```
Use it
```
$raw  = file_get_contents($path);
$chip = chipParse($raw);

$title  = chipGet($chip, 'title', 'untitled');
$author = chipGet($chip, 'author', '');
$body   = chipGet($chip, 'body', '');

loadContent('body', '<h1>' . htmlspecialchars($title) . '</h1>');
loadContent('body', '<p class="by">' . htmlspecialchars($author) . '</p>');
loadContent('body', '<div class="post">' . nl2br(htmlspecialchars($body)) . '</div>');
```
That’s fetching a particular unit: chipGet($chip, 'title').

───

After you read the file into $raw and split once:
```
// $meta = array of key => value from BETWEEN the --- lines only
// $body = everything AFTER the second ---

$name  = $meta['name']  ?? '';   // contact
$email = $meta['email'] ?? '';
// message might be $meta['message'] OR $body — you choose one convention

// from a leaf chip on Sophia:
$paperName = $meta['name'] ?? '';  // wait — nested "chip: name:" is harder
```
---

Find which chip (registry without a registry)
```
~storage/STAR-LUX/posts/post-001.chip
~storage/STAR-LUX/posts/post-002.chip
~storage/STAR-LUX/mail/msg-....chip

// by filename (id in the name)
$path = STORAGE_ROOT . '/' . Space_Slug . '/posts/' . $safeId . '.chip';

// by scanning for a meta field (slow, fine for dozens)
foreach (glob($dir . '/*.chip') as $f) {
  $c = chipParse(file_get_contents($f));
  if (chipGet($c, 'type') === 'post' && chipGet($c, 'id') === $want) {
    // found
  }
}
```
When you have hundreds, you can add a dumb index later (index.chip listing ids). Not day one.